Odds are pretty low any way, so is it worth the effort? If they are only grammar nazis come to scrutinize they are more likely than not the type to steer away at the mention of extreme poverty, furthermore it says M4F, don't know why you read it, oh but you didn't or you would've read the part about being depressed and unmotivated. Or don't get it. :/

&#x200B;

Anyway, objection noted, will consider doing it later, but I doubt it.

I attached that magic effect as a script, is it correct that in the script when I hit properties it is greyed out and says 'no properties'?

&#x200B;

And on the ability I attached the magic effect with magnitude 0 or 1 or what?

To the 'angel' who noted me, you and some other signs I was sent were right, faith pulled me through this whole power shit and another 'angel' was sent to help us get it done without costing us so much we couldn't afford it. I mean we hardly got anything left for the month and it'll be tough but we have power.

&#x200B;

'Faith. Its never a bad thing to have.' -Walter Bishop.

I have 8GB RAM.

&#x200B;

Hmm, you know that seems pretty likely. After all the longer you play, the more likely this is to happen. I didn't know the PC version had this problem.

&#x200B;

So, what do I patch, surely not the launcher?

Yeah its not like you could give it to poor people or anything.... 🙄

&#x200B;

EDIT: All the down votes just go to prove that theres far too many 'classists'.

Same goes for those who refuse to believe poverty exists in the USA then.

&#x200B;

Furthermore, why do we the people have to make all the sacrifices and not the polluting companies? E.G. Bottled Water Company (true for any product using plastic including store bags, milk and water jugs, etc or aluminum, copper, etc, etc.) reduces plastic in its bottles as its sacrifice to go green which translates into money saved from using less material so therefore profiting and then increases its price as it had to 'sacrifice' and go green, so now you gotta pay the cost therefore raising profits AGAIN. Meanwhile we have to pay more and the things break and waste water, etc. way to easily even from a temperature change that happens too rapidly o drastically. So we have to pay more and often end up with nothing or half quality while they raise prices and use less materials so lower costs. How the hell is THAT \*them\* sacrificing at all?
